IMPORT prelude

-- Civil Law Act 1909 (Singapore) -- wagering contracts (s 5), maintenance, champerty and third-party funding (ss 5A, 5B),
-- contracts that must be evidenced in writing (s 6), contribution between wrongdoers (s 15), claims for a death and
-- bereavement (ss 20 to 22), the survivorship presumption (s 30), contracts and proceedings by 18-to-20-year-olds (ss 35, 36),
-- and the standard of care for medical advice (s 37).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CLA1909.txt. The
-- deposit's arrangement of sections runs out of step with the body; the encoding follows the body.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 18 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository (s 5 by 6, s 20 by 4). It is a
-- miscellany; this row takes the provisions an ordinary person relies on. Not encoded: law and equity, insolvency rules
-- (s 4), Bain v Fothergill, European monetary union, interest (s 12), charges over choses in action, the abolished
-- husband's liability, perpetuities and accumulations, and the trust and estate sections.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Civil Law Act 1909 -- core`

§§ `5 -- wagers`

-- s 5(1): "All contracts or agreements ... by way of gaming or wagering shall be null and void." (2): no action to recover
-- winnings. (3A): except gaming and betting by exempted or licensed operators (Singapore Pools, the turf club, Gambling
-- Control Act licensees). (3E): but the exception never covers LENDING money or giving CREDIT for gambling. (4), (5): nor does
-- s 5 touch an "investment activity" -- futures, options, contracts for differences, swaps -- entered into by way of business.
-- (6): a promise to repay money paid under a void wager, or a commission for one, is itself void.
DECLARE Bet IS ONE OF
    `a private bet between friends`
    `a bet with a licensed operator`
    `credit extended by a licensed operator for betting`
    `a contract for differences entered into by way of business`
    `a prize for a lawful sporting competition`

GIVEN `the bet` IS A Bet
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contract is enforceable despite section 5` IF
    CONSIDER `the bet`
    WHEN `a bet with a licensed operator` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a contract for differences entered into by way of business` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a prize for a lawful sporting competition` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `5A, 5B -- litigation funding`

-- s 5A(1): no one is liable in tort for maintenance or champerty. (2): but such contracts may still be contrary to public
-- policy, subject to s 5B. s 5B(2): a contract with a QUALIFYING third-party funder for PRESCRIBED dispute resolution
-- proceedings "is not contrary to public policy or otherwise illegal". (4): if the funder stops qualifying or breaches the
-- prescribed requirements, its rights under the contract become unenforceable; (5), (6) subject to relief for accident or
-- inadvertence or on just and equitable grounds.
GIVEN `the funder is qualifying` IS A BOOLEAN, `the proceedings are prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the funder complied with the requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the funder can enforce the funding contract` IF
    `the funder is qualifying` AND `the proceedings are prescribed` AND `the funder complied with the requirements`

§§ `6 -- contracts that must be in writing`

-- s 6: no action on (a) an executor's promise to pay from their own estate; (b) "any special promise to answer for the debt,
-- default or miscarriage of another person" (a guarantee); (c) an agreement in consideration of marriage; (d) "any contract for
-- the sale or other disposition of immovable property, or any interest in such property"; or (e) "any agreement that is not to
-- be performed within the space of one year", "unless the promise or agreement ... or some memorandum or note thereof, is IN
-- WRITING AND SIGNED by the party to be charged".
--
-- With the Electronic Transactions Act: s 6(d) is the rule requiring writing for dispositions of immovable property, and the
-- ETA First Schedule takes exactly those dispositions out of Part 2 of that Act. A lease that s 6(d) requires to be signed cannot
-- be signed electronically under the ETA (see the electronic-transactions-act-2010 row, finding 3).
DECLARE Agreement IS ONE OF
    `a guarantee`
    `a sale of land`
    `a lease`
    `a contract lasting more than a year`
    `a sale of goods to be completed next week`
    `an agreement in consideration of marriage`

GIVEN `the agreement` IS AN Agreement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement must be evidenced in signed writing` IF
    CONSIDER `the agreement`
    WHEN `a sale of goods to be completed next week` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the agreement` IS AN Agreement, `signed writing exists` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an action can be brought on the agreement` IF
    (NOT `the agreement must be evidenced in signed writing` `the agreement`) OR `signed writing exists`

§§ `15 -- contribution`

-- s 15(1): a person liable for damage may recover contribution from anyone else liable for the same damage. (3): a contributor
-- remains liable even after ceasing to be liable to the victim -- UNLESS that was by the expiry of a limitation period that
-- extinguished the right. (4): a person who settles "in bona fide settlement or compromise" may recover contribution "without
-- regard to whether or not he himself is or ever was liable", if he would have been liable on the facts alleged.
-- (Limitation Act 1959 s 6A: 2 years from the judgment or settlement.)
DECLARE ContributionClaim HAS
    `the claimant settled in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant would have been liable on the facts alleged` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant was actually liable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other party's liability was extinguished by limitation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other party was liable for the same damage` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the claim` IS A ContributionClaim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `contribution can be recovered` IF
        `the claim`'s `the other party was liable for the same damage`
    AND NOT `the claim`'s `the other party's liability was extinguished by limitation`
    AND (    `the claim`'s `the claimant was actually liable`
         OR  (`the claim`'s `the claimant settled in good faith` AND `the claim`'s `the claimant would have been liable on the facts alleged`))

§§ `20 to 22 -- death claims and bereavement`

-- s 20(8): a "dependant" is "(a) the wife or husband or FORMER WIFE of the deceased; (b) any parent, grandparent or great-
-- grandparent; (c) any child, grandchild or great-grandchild; (d) a child of the family; and (e) any person who is, or is the
-- issue of, a brother, sister, uncle or aunt". (9): affinity counts as blood, half blood as whole, stepchildren as children.
-- (5): one action, "within 3 years after the death".
-- s 21(4): bereavement damages are $15,000, for (2) the spouse; if none, the children; if none, the parents; if none (for a
-- minor), a step-parent; if none, the siblings -- each class only if no earlier class exists. (5): shared equally.
-- s 22(1): insurance, CPF and pensions on death are not deducted. (3): a WIDOW's remarriage or prospects are disregarded.
-- (3A): a former wife recovers only for a subsisting maintenance order.
--
-- A former WIFE is a dependant; a former HUSBAND is not. A widow's remarriage prospects are ignored; nothing is said of a
-- widower's.
DECLARE Relation IS ONE OF
    `wife`
    `husband`
    `former wife`
    `former husband`
    `parent`
    `child`
    `grandchild`
    `cousin`
    `nephew or niece`
    `friend`

GIVEN `the relation` IS A Relation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a dependant` IF
    CONSIDER `the relation`
    WHEN `former husband` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `friend` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- (A cousin is "the issue of ... [an] uncle or aunt" under s 20(8)(e).)

DECLARE Survivors HAS
    `a spouse survives` IS A BOOLEAN
    `children survive` IS A NUMBER
    `parents survive` IS A NUMBER
    `siblings survive` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the survivors` IS A Survivors
GIVETH A STRING
`who takes bereavement damages` MEANS
    IF `the survivors`'s `a spouse survives` THEN "the spouse"
    ELSE IF `the survivors`'s `children survive` GREATER THAN 0 THEN "the children"
         ELSE IF `the survivors`'s `parents survive` GREATER THAN 0 THEN "the parents"
              ELSE IF `the survivors`'s `siblings survive` GREATER THAN 0 THEN "the siblings"
                   ELSE "no one"

GIVEN `the survivors` IS A Survivors
GIVETH A NUMBER
`each person's share of bereavement damages` MEANS
    IF `the survivors`'s `a spouse survives` THEN 15000
    ELSE IF `the survivors`'s `children survive` GREATER THAN 0 THEN 15000 DIVIDED BY `the survivors`'s `children survive`
         ELSE IF `the survivors`'s `parents survive` GREATER THAN 0 THEN 15000 DIVIDED BY `the survivors`'s `parents survive`
              ELSE IF `the survivors`'s `siblings survive` GREATER THAN 0 THEN 15000 DIVIDED BY `the survivors`'s `siblings survive`
                   ELSE 0

GIVEN `years since death` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the death claim is in time` IF
    `years since death` AT MOST 3

§§ `30 -- who died first`

-- s 30: where two or more die "in circumstances rendering it uncertain which of them survived", for title to property the deaths
-- are "presumed to have occurred in order of seniority and accordingly the YOUNGER shall be deemed to have survived the elder".
GIVEN `age of A` IS A NUMBER, `age of B` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A STRING
`who is deemed to have survived` MEANS
    IF `age of A` LESS THAN `age of B` THEN "A" ELSE "B"

§§ `35, 36 -- 18 to 20`

-- s 35(1): a contract by a minor who has attained 18 "shall have effect as if he were of full age". (4): EXCEPT (a) a sale,
-- purchase, mortgage, assignment or settlement of land, other than a lease of up to 3 years; (b) a lease of more than 3 years;
-- (c) dealings with a beneficial interest under a trust; (d) settling the minor's own claims.
-- s 36: an 18-year-old may bring or defend the Scheduled proceedings in their own name, and is not under a disability for
-- limitation purposes in them.
DECLARE YoungContract IS ONE OF
    `a phone contract`
    `a car loan`
    `a two-year flat lease`
    `a five-year lease`
    `buying a flat`
    `selling a trust interest`
    `settling a personal injury claim`

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER, `the contract` IS A YoungContract
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contract binds as if of full age` IF
        `age` AT LEAST 21
    OR  (    `age` AT LEAST 18
         AND CONSIDER `the contract`
             WHEN `a five-year lease` THEN FALSE
             WHEN `buying a flat` THEN FALSE
             WHEN `selling a trust interest` THEN FALSE
             WHEN `settling a personal injury claim` THEN FALSE
             OTHERWISE TRUE)

§§ `37 -- medical advice`

-- s 37(1): a healthcare professional meets the standard of care in giving medical advice if the way they acted is accepted by a
-- respectable body of medical opinion as reasonable AND that opinion is LOGICAL. (2): but that peer opinion may be relied on only
-- if it requires the patient to have been given (a)(i) information a person in the patient's circumstances would reasonably
-- require, AND (ii) information the professional knows or ought to know is material to THIS patient -- including for "an
-- idiosyncratic reason"; and (b) supports withholding either only where there is "reasonable justification".
-- Illustration (c): believing the patient would be dissuaded by the risks "by itself, does not give ... reasonable
-- justification" for not telling them.
DECLARE Advice HAS
    `accepted by a respectable body of medical opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that opinion is logical` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gave the information a reasonable patient would require` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gave information known to matter to this patient` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonable justification for any withholding` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the advice` IS AN Advice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the standard of care is met` IF
        `the advice`'s `accepted by a respectable body of medical opinion`
    AND `the advice`'s `that opinion is logical`
    AND (    (`the advice`'s `gave the information a reasonable patient would require` AND `the advice`'s `gave information known to matter to this patient`)
         OR  `the advice`'s `reasonable justification for any withholding`)

DECLARE Reason IS ONE OF
    `an emergency with no one to consent`
    `the patient expressly waived the information`
    `the doctor thought the patient would refuse if told`

GIVEN `the reason` IS A Reason
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reason justifies withholding` IF
    CONSIDER `the reason`
    WHEN `the doctor thought the patient would refuse if told` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
